.TH PODRUNNER 1 "" "podrunner" "podrunner manual"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
podrunner \- A static launcher that runs CI jobs in one fresh unit for each
job
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpodrunner COMMAND [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBRun the slots:\fR
.TP
\fBserve\fR
Run the slots: one tick each second, and the control socket
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
Check a configuration as serve does before it starts, and start nothing
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
Write a configuration file
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
The inputs of a host check, or the checks of a local run
.TP
\fBprint\-unit\fR
Print a unit of systemd for serve, with no credential
.TP
\fBinstall\-unit\fR
Install the unit of the system and start it, as root
.TP
\fBremove\-unit\fR
Stop and remove the unit of the system, as root
.PP
\fBControl a serve:\fR
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
The state of the slots of serve
.TP
\fBdrain\fR
Take no new job; the jobs in flight go on
.TP
\fBresume\fR
The source takes jobs again
.TP
\fBstop\fR
Drain, then end when each job is final
.TP
\fBclear\-degraded\fR
Start jobs again after a residue
.TP
\fBsource\fR
Control one source of serve
.PP
\fBRun a workflow on this host:\fR
.TP
\fBrun\fR
Run the jobs of a workflow on this host, with no forge
.PP
\fBCheck and sign:\fR
.TP
\fBaudit\fR
Check the audit file of serve
.TP
\fBimage\fR
Check a file of the official runner
.TP
\fBpin\-sign\fR
Print the signer and the signature of the pin list
.PP
\fBThe mint and the source programs:\fR
.TP
\fBmint\-serve\fR
Run the remote mint, on a machine with no unit
.TP
\fBfake\-source\fR
A fake source on stdio, for a test of a program source
.TP
\fBsource\-conformance\fR
Run the tests of the source wire against a source program
.PP
\fBRead the manual:\fR
.TP
\fBman\fR
Print the manual: through a pager on a terminal, else as text
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Print the version and the commit
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help.
.SH DESCRIPTION
podrunner runs CI jobs. For each job it starts one fresh unit, runs the
official runner once in it, and destroys the unit.
.PP
serve takes jobs from the sources of a configuration file. run runs the jobs
of one workflow file on this host, with no forge.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "podrunner serve"
Run the slots: one tick each second, and the control socket.
.PP
SIGTERM and SIGINT start the drain of stop.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner serve \-\-config FILE \-\-state DIR [\-\-socket PATH]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file of serve (podrunner.toml).
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket. Default: DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner check"
Check a configuration as serve does before it starts, and start nothing.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner check \-\-config FILE [\-\-here]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file of serve or of mint\-serve.
.TP
\fB\-\-here\fR
Fail when a unit kind of the file cannot run on this host.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner status"
The state of the slots of serve.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner status [\-\-json] (\-\-state DIR | \-\-socket PATH)\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the status as JSON (status.v1).
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket of serve.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-socket.
.SS "podrunner drain"
Take no new job; the jobs in flight go on.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner drain [\-\-source NAME] (\-\-state DIR | \-\-socket PATH)\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fINAME\fR
Only the source NAME of the configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket of serve.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-socket.
.SS "podrunner resume"
The source takes jobs again.
.PP
A stopped source is built again from its table first.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner resume \-\-source NAME (\-\-state DIR | \-\-socket PATH)\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fINAME\fR
Only the source NAME of the configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket of serve.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-socket.
.SS "podrunner stop"
Drain, then end when each job is final.
.PP
With \-\-wait, stop also waits until serve has ended. A timeout exits 75.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner stop ([\-\-source NAME] (\-\-state DIR | \-\-socket PATH) | \-\-wait \-\-state DIR [\-\-timeout SECONDS])\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fINAME\fR
Only the source NAME of the configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket of serve.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until serve has ended: the lock of DIR is free.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR
The longest wait of \-\-wait.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-socket.
.PP
\-\-timeout needs \-\-wait.
.PP
\-\-wait needs \-\-state.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-wait, \-\-source.
.SS "podrunner clear\-degraded"
Start jobs again after a residue.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner clear\-degraded (\-\-state DIR | \-\-socket PATH)\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket of serve.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-socket.
.SS "podrunner config"
Write a configuration file.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner config COMMAND [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBCommands:\fR
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Write a podrunner.toml for serve from the unit kinds of this host
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner config init"
Write a podrunner.toml for serve from the unit kinds of this host.
.PP
A second run with the same input changes nothing. A file OUT with another text
exits 77.
.PP
When no unit kind runs on this host, or check refuses the file, the exit is
78.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner config init \-\-source NAME \-\-program PATH [\-\-arg ARG]... [\-\-key\-file FILE] [\-\-tier trusted|untrusted] [\-\-org LOGIN]... [\-\-user LOGIN]... \-\-podvm PATH \-\-images STORE [\-\-podnet PATH] \-\-image NAME@sha256:HEX \-\-built\-at\-s N [\-\-runner\-version V] [\-\-unpacked\-bytes N] [\-\-slots N] [\-\-kinds auto|LIST] [\-\-host NAME] \-\-out FILE [\-\-json]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fINAME\fR
The name of the program source.
.TP
\fB\-\-program\fR \fIPATH\fR
The source program.
.TP
\fB\-\-arg\fR \fIARG\fR
An argument of the program.
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
The key file of the program.
.TP
\fB\-\-tier\fR \fITIER\fR
The tier of the source: trusted or untrusted. Default: trusted.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fILOGIN\fR
An organization that the source serves.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fILOGIN\fR
A user that the source serves.
.TP
\fB\-\-podvm\fR \fIPATH\fR
The podvm binary.
.TP
\fB\-\-images\fR \fISTORE\fR
The image store of podvm.
.TP
\fB\-\-podnet\fR \fIPATH\fR
The podnet binary: the egress hold of the podvm kind.
.TP
\fB\-\-image\fR \fINAME@sha256:HEX\fR
The runner image, pinned by digest.
.TP
\fB\-\-built\-at\-s\fR \fIN\fR
The build time of the image, in seconds since 1970.
.TP
\fB\-\-runner\-version\fR \fIV\fR
The version of the runner in the image.
.TP
\fB\-\-unpacked\-bytes\fR \fIN\fR
The size of the image when it is unpacked.
.TP
\fB\-\-slots\fR \fIN\fR
The slots of each unit kind. Default: 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-kinds\fR \fILIST\fR
auto, or a comma list of microvm, incus and podvm. Default: auto.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fINAME\fR
The name of the host. Default: the host name of the kernel.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR
The file to write, at mode 0600.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one line of JSON: the file, the kinds, the refused kinds, and whether it
changed.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner source"
Control one source of serve.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner source COMMAND [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBCommands:\fR
.TP
\fBrestart\fR
Build one source again with a new key, and keep its jobs
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner source restart"
Build one source again with a new key, and keep its jobs.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner source restart \-\-name NAME (\-\-state DIR | \-\-socket PATH)\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
The source to build again.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory of serve. Its control socket is DIR/ctl.sock.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR
The control socket of serve.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-socket.
.SS "podrunner doctor"
The inputs of a host check, or the checks of a local run.
.PP
With \-\-run, doctor takes each option of run: podrunner run \-\-help.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner doctor [\-\-config FILE] [\-\-json] | [\-\-json] \-\-run FILE [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file of serve: check its unit kinds and sources too.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR \fIFILE\fR
The workflow file of a local run: check the host for it.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give only one of \-\-config, \-\-run.
.SS "podrunner audit"
Check the audit file of serve.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner audit COMMAND [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBCommands:\fR
.TP
\fBverify\fR
Check the chain of audit.jsonl
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner audit verify"
Check the chain of audit.jsonl.
.PP
A lost, changed or torn line exits 76.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner audit verify (\-\-state DIR | \-\-file FILE) [\-\-anchor SEQ:HASH]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory: check DIR/audit.jsonl.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
The audit file to check.
.TP
\fB\-\-anchor\fR \fISEQ:HASH\fR
The seq of a line and the prev of the next line in the copy at the source.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-state, \-\-file.
.SS "podrunner print\-unit"
Print a unit of systemd for serve, with no credential.
.PP
With no \-\-system, the unit is a user unit.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner print\-unit [\-\-system [\-\-user NAME]] \-\-config FILE \-\-state DIR [\-\-binary PATH] [\-\-watchdog SECONDS]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
A unit of the system, not a user unit.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fINAME\fR
With \-\-system: the account that runs serve. Default: podrunner.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file, as an absolute path.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory, as an absolute path.
.TP
\fB\-\-binary\fR \fIPATH\fR
The absolute path of podrunner in the unit. Default: /usr/local/bin/podrunner.
.TP
\fB\-\-watchdog\fR \fISECONDS\fR
The watchdog of systemd: serve tells systemd at half of this time.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
\-\-user needs \-\-system.
.SS "podrunner install\-unit"
Install the unit of the system and start it, as root.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner install\-unit \-\-system [\-\-user NAME] \-\-config FILE \-\-state DIR [\-\-binary PATH] [\-\-watchdog SECONDS]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
A unit of the system, not a user unit.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fINAME\fR
With \-\-system: the account that runs serve. Default: podrunner.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file, as an absolute path.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
The state directory, as an absolute path.
.TP
\fB\-\-binary\fR \fIPATH\fR
The absolute path of podrunner in the unit. Default: /usr/local/bin/podrunner.
.TP
\fB\-\-watchdog\fR \fISECONDS\fR
The watchdog of systemd: serve tells systemd at half of this time.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner remove\-unit"
Stop and remove the unit of the system, as root.
.PP
The state directory and the configuration stay.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner remove\-unit \-\-system\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
The unit of the system.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner pin\-sign"
Print the signer and the signature of the pin list.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner pin\-sign \-\-config FILE \-\-seed\-file FILE\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file of serve (podrunner.toml).
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
The seed: 64 hex digits, mode 0600.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner mint\-serve"
Run the remote mint, on a machine with no unit.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner mint\-serve \-\-config FILE\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
The configuration file of the mint.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner fake\-source"
A fake source on stdio, for a test of a program source.
.PP
It ends when stdin ends.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner fake\-source [\-\-script FILE]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-script\fR \fIFILE\fR
The script of the fake source.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner source\-conformance"
Run the tests of the source wire against a source program.
.PP
Exit 0 when each test passes, else 1.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner source\-conformance [\-\-json] \-\- PROGRAM [ARG...]\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIPROGRAM\fR
The source program.
.TP
\fI[ARG]...\fR
The arguments of the program.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object for each line.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner image"
Check a file of the official runner.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner image COMMAND [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBCommands:\fR
.TP
\fBverify\fR
Check actions\-runner\-linux\-ARCH\-VERSION.tar.gz against its pin
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner image verify"
Check actions\-runner\-linux\-ARCH\-VERSION.tar.gz against its pin.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner image verify \-\-tarball FILE \-\-arch ARCH\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-tarball\fR \fIFILE\fR
The release tarball of the official runner.
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fIARCH\fR
x64 or arm64. x86_64 and aarch64 are the same.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SS "podrunner run"
Run the jobs of a workflow on this host, with no forge.
.PP
Each option is in https://github.com/PodUtils/podrunner/blob/main/docs/cli.md,
in the row of podrunner run.
.PP
A key of run.toml is an option with no dashes. Exit 0, or 1 when a job failed.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner run (FILE | DIR) (\-\-runner\-dir DIR | (\-\-podvm PATH [\-\-podnet PATH | \-\-vnet PATH] | \-\-microvm PATH [\-\-engine DIR] | \-\-incus PATH [\-\-engine DIR]) \-\-images STORE \-\-image NAME@sha256:HEX) [OPTION...]\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
The workflow file, or a directory of workflow files.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-runner\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
An unpacked release of the official runner. Each job runs in it as the user of
podrunner.
.TP
\fB\-\-podvm\fR \fIPATH\fR
The podvm binary. Each job runs in a fresh podvm unit.
.TP
\fB\-\-podnet\fR \fIPATH\fR
With \-\-podvm: hold each unit under podnet pod.
.TP
\fB\-\-vnet\fR \fIPATH\fR
With \-\-podvm: run the runner of each unit under the vnet shim of this
podnet.
.TP
\fB\-\-microvm\fR \fIPATH\fR
The podvm binary. Each job runs in a fresh guest of the microvm kind.
.TP
\fB\-\-incus\fR \fIPATH\fR
The podvm binary. Each job runs in a fresh incus instance.
.TP
\fB\-\-engine\fR \fIDIR\fR
With \-\-microvm or \-\-incus: the container engine of each guest.
.TP
\fB\-\-images\fR \fISTORE\fR
The image store of podvm.
.TP
\fB\-\-image\fR \fINAME@sha256:HEX\fR
The runner image of each unit, pinned by digest.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\fR \fIHOST\fR
A host that a step can reach through the egress module.
.TP
\fB\-\-platform\fR \fILABEL=TARGET\fR
Map a label of runs\-on to a runner image NAME@sha256:HEX, or to host.
.TP
\fB\-\-actions\fR \fIDIR\fR
The store of the actions. Default: XDG_CACHE_HOME/podrunner/actions.
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Use the lock file and the store only, and fetch nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-frozen\fR
Refuse a change of the lock file.
.TP
\fB\-\-artifacts\fR \fIDIR\fR
Keep the artifacts of the run in DIR.
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\fR \fIDIR\fR
The store of the cache service. Default: XDG_CACHE_HOME/podrunner/cache.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
No cache: each lookup is a miss, and each save is refused.
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\fR \fINAME\fR
A secret from the variable NAME of the environment. A value in argv is
refused.
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
A file of secrets, one NAME=VALUE on each line, at mode 0600 or less.
.TP
\fB\-\-github\-token\-env\fR \fINAME\fR
Give the token of the variable NAME to each job whose permissions are not
empty.
.TP
\fB\-\-job\fR \fIID\fR
Run the job ID and each job that it needs. With \-\-rerun: run that job again.
.TP
\fB\-\-matrix\fR \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Keep only the matrix cells with this value.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
Print each job with its name, runs\-on and needs.
.TP
\fB\-\-graph\fR
Print the stages of needs and each edge.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\fR
Parse the file and print each warning.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Resolve the pins and build the job message of each cell, with no unit.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Do not write the new lines of each job log to stderr.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Write one JSON object for each log line and for the end of each job.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Keep the logs of each job in DIR.
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\-secret\-file\fR \fINAME=FILE\fR
The secrets of the environment NAME, from FILE at mode 0600.
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\-var\-file\fR \fINAME=FILE\fR
The vars of the environment NAME, from FILE.
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\-allow\fR \fINAME=HOST\fR
A host that the jobs of the environment NAME can reach.
.TP
\fB\-\-protected\fR \fINAME\fR
Mark the environment NAME as protected: its jobs need an approval.
.TP
\fB\-\-approve\fR \fINAME\fR
Approve the protected environment NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR \fIDIR\fR
Copy the workspace of each job to DIR/JOB.N after the job.
.TP
\fB\-\-toolcache\fR \fIDIR\fR
With \-\-podvm: a tool cache, read\-only in each unit.
.TP
\fB\-\-local\-repository\fR \fIOWNER/REPO@REF=DIR\fR
Serve the files of DIR as that reference of an action.
.TP
\fB\-\-action\-server\fR \fIURL\fR
The forge of the actions in place of https://github.com.
.TP
\fB\-\-oidc\-issuer\fR \fIURL\fR
The issuer of the OIDC tokens. Default: https://oidc.podrunner.invalid.
.TP
\fB\-\-oidc\-keys\fR \fIFILE\fR
Write the public keys of the OIDC tokens to FILE.
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR
Run again after each change of the tree or of the workflow file.
.TP
\fB\-\-schedule\fR
Run at each time of the crons of on.schedule, again and again.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-config\fR
Read no configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-\-changed\-since\fR \fIREF\fR
The changed files for the paths filters: the files that differ from REF.
.TP
\fB\-\-web\fR \fIIP:PORT\fR
Serve a web view of the run on an address of the loopback.
.TP
\fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
With a unit kind: run up to N jobs at a time, each in its own unit. Default:
1.
.TP
\fB\-\-break\fR \fIJOB:STEP\fR
Pause before the step STEP of the job JOB.
.TP
\fB\-\-break\-on\-failure\fR
Pause after the first failed step of each job.
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-failed\fR
The same as \-\-break\-on\-failure.
.TP
\fB\-\-checkout\fR \fIDIR\fR
The tree of actions/checkout. Default: the git tree of the current directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-checkout\-head\fR
With \-\-checkout: the committed files of HEAD only.
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-git\fR
With \-\-checkout: give the checkout a .git, and fail out of a git tree.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-git\fR
With \-\-checkout: give the checkout no .git.
.TP
\fB\-\-event\fR \fINAME\fR
The event of the run. Default: push.
.TP
\fB\-\-event\-path\fR \fIFILE\fR
The JSON payload of the event.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-event\fR
Run the workflow also when its on: does not take the event.
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fINAME\fR
The git remote that gives github.repository. Default: origin.
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fIREF\fR
The value of github.ref.
.TP
\fB\-\-sha\fR \fISHA\fR
The value of github.sha: 40 or 64 hex digits.
.TP
\fB\-\-repository\fR \fIOWNER/REPO\fR
The value of github.repository.
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR \fINAME\fR
The value of github.actor.
.TP
\fB\-\-var\fR \fINAME=VALUE\fR
A value of vars.
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fINAME=VALUE\fR
A value of inputs.
.TP
\fB\-\-var\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
A file of vars, in the syntax of GITHUB_ENV.
.TP
\fB\-\-input\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
A file of inputs, in the syntax of GITHUB_ENV.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fINAME=VALUE\fR
A variable of the environment of each job.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
A file of variables of each job, in the syntax of GITHUB_ENV.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fIDIR\fR
Keep the run in DIR: its state, its logs and its artifacts.
.TP
\fB\-\-rerun\fR \fIDIR\fR
Run the failed cells of the run in DIR again, and each job after them.
.TP
\fB\-\-failed\fR
With \-\-rerun: run the failed cells, not the jobs of \-\-job.
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
With \-\-rerun: accept a workflow that changed since the run.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give only one of \-\-podvm, \-\-microvm, \-\-incus.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-podnet, \-\-vnet.
.PP
\-\-podnet needs \-\-podvm.
.PP
\-\-vnet needs \-\-podvm.
.PP
\-\-toolcache needs \-\-podvm.
.PP
\-\-engine needs one of \-\-microvm, \-\-incus.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-list, \-\-graph, \-\-validate, \-\-dry\-run.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-watch, \-\-schedule.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-web, \-\-dry\-run.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-offline, \-\-frozen.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-cache, \-\-no\-cache.
.PP
\-\-checkout\-head needs \-\-checkout.
.PP
\-\-with\-git needs \-\-checkout.
.PP
\-\-no\-git needs \-\-checkout.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-with\-git, \-\-no\-git.
.PP
\-\-failed needs \-\-rerun.
.PP
\-\-refresh needs \-\-rerun.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-failed, \-\-job.
.SS "podrunner man"
Print the manual: through a pager on a terminal, else as text.
.PP
A SECTION is a command, such as run or config init, or environment or
exit\-status.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner man [SECTION...] [\-\-no\-pager | \-\-json | \-\-roff]\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fI[SECTION]...\fR
A command or a topic of the manual.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print the text with no pager.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the manual as JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-roff\fR
Print the manual as a man page (man 7).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give only one of \-\-json, \-\-roff.
.SS "podrunner version"
Print the version and the commit.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodrunner version [OPTIONS]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
\fBThe local mode:\fR
.TP
\fBHOME\fR
The home: the place of the user files and stores of run when XDG is not set.
Used by: run.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
The directory of the user file podrunner/run.toml. Used by: run.
.TP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
The directory of the default stores of run: actions, cache and concurrency.
Used by: run.
.TP
\fBGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT\fR
Set to 0 for each call of git: git asks for no password. Used by: run.
podrunner sets it and does not read it.
.PP
\fBserve and its sources:\fR
.TP
\fBNOTIFY_SOCKET\fR
The socket of systemd: serve sends READY=1 and STOPPING=1 to it. Used by:
serve.
.TP
\fBWATCHDOG_USEC\fR
The watchdog of systemd: serve sends WATCHDOG=1 at half of it. Used by: serve.
.TP
\fBWATCHDOG_PID\fR
The process that the watchdog of systemd watches. Used by: serve.
.TP
\fBGITHUB_ACTIONS_FORCE_GHES\fR
When it is set, a source takes its forge as GitHub Enterprise Server, as
actions/scaleset does. Used by: serve.
.PP
\fBThe unit kinds:\fR
.TP
\fBPODVM_STORE\fR
The image store of podvm, set for each call of podvm. podrunner sets it and
does not read it.
.TP
\fBPODVM_INCUS_SOCKET\fR
The socket of incusd, as podvm finds it. Used by: doctor.
.TP
\fBINCUS_DIR\fR
With no PODVM_INCUS_SOCKET: the directory of the socket of incusd. Used by:
doctor.
.TP
\fBPODRUNNER_UNIT_TAG\fR
The tag of a unit of the host kinds: it finds each process of the unit.
podrunner sets it and does not read it.
.TP
\fBPODRUNNER_CONFINE_CANARY\fR
The mark of the process that the self\-test of the confine layer starts. Used
by: serve. podrunner sets it and does not read it.
.PP
\fBThe pager:\fR
.TP
\fBPAGER\fR
The pager of the manual on a terminal. An empty value or cat writes the text
with no pager. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBTERM\fR
With no PAGER, less is used only when TERM names a terminal that is not dumb.
Used by: man.
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
The directories where the probe looks for less. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBLINES\fR
The lines of a screen of the built\-in pager, when the terminal size is not
known. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBLESS\fR
The options of less. When it is not set, the pager sets FRX. Used by: man.
podrunner reads it and sets it.
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBDIR/ctl.sock\fR
The control socket of serve, at mode 0600, in its state directory.
.TP
\fBDIR/serve.lock\fR
The lock of the state directory: one serve at a time.
.TP
\fBDIR/audit.jsonl\fR
The audit file of serve: a chain of lines.
.TP
\fBpodrunner\-actions.lock\fR
The pins of the actions and images of a workflow, beside the workflow file.
.TP
\fB\&.secrets\fR
The secrets of a local run, in the checkout tree or the current directory.
.SH "THE KEYS OF RUN.TOML"
XDG_CONFIG_HOME/podrunner/run.toml of the user, then .podrunner/run.toml of
the project. Each key is a flag of run with no dashes. A flag of the command
line wins.
.TP
