.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR (success)
The command did its work.
.TP
\fB1\fR (failed)
A job of run failed, a check of doctor \-\-run failed, or a test of
source\-conformance failed.
.TP
\fB64\fR (usage)
A value of the command line cannot be used.
.TP
\fB66\fR (notfound)
A path or a name does not exist.
.TP
\fB69\fR (unavailable)
A service or a path is not available.
.TP
\fB75\fR (tempfail, timeout)
A service refused for now. A later try can work. A wait ended at its time
limit.
.TP
\fB76\fR (protocol)
The far end broke the protocol.
.TP
\fB77\fR (refused)
The far end refused the credentials or the identity.
.TP
\fB78\fR (config, revoked, suite)
A configuration cannot be used. A credential that worked is gone. A restart
does not help. The far end and this end have no protocol or suite in common.
.TP
\fB80\fR (unsupported)
The host, the build or the far end does not support the action.
.TP
\fB130\fR (interrupted)
A signal ended a local run.
